IMPORT prelude

-- National Disability Insurance Scheme Act 2013 (Cth) -- becoming a participant in the NDIS, and ceasing to be one: the
-- access request and the access criteria (ss 18, 21); the age requirements (s 22); the residence requirements, with the
-- protected SCV holder worked out (s 23; s 9); the disability requirements (s 24); the early intervention requirements, with
-- developmental delay worked out (s 25; s 9); what the participant's notice says (s 28); the time the CEO has to decide, the
-- deemed refusal and the deemed withdrawal (ss 20, 21(3), 26); review of the access decision (s 100(2), (5)); a fresh access
-- request (s 19(2)); when a participant ceases to be one -- death, aged care first begun after 65, revocation, withdrawal
-- (s 29); withdrawing (s 29A); and revocation (s 30(1), (5), (6)).
--
-- SEAT: the person with disability -- here Jake Harding after his stroke at 56 -- asking "Am I eligible to become a
-- participant, and what happens to my participation when I turn 65 or go into aged care?". Every decision is phrased as that
-- person asks it. Where the Act addresses the CEO ("the CEO must decide ...", "the CEO may revoke ...") it is encoded as what
-- the person can expect: when they are taken to be refused, what their notice must say, when their status may be taken away.
-- Where the Act hands a judgment to the CEO -- that the person resides in Australia (s 23(2)), that episodic impairments are
-- taken to be permanent (s 24(3)), the s 25(1)(b)-(d) satisfactions, that non-compliance was reasonable (ss 26(3), 30(6)) --
-- it is asked as an input: "if the CEO is satisfied that ...".
--
-- Provisions covered: ss 9 (child, developmental delay, protected SCV holder), 18, 19(2), 20, 21, 22, 23(1) (with (2) as the
-- matters the CEO weighs, asked), 24(1)-(3), 25(1), (1A), (2), 26(2), (3), 28(1), (2), 29(1), (2), 29A(3), (5), 30(1), (5),
-- (6), 100(2), (5).
--
-- Edition: Compilation No. 26, compilation date 27 August 2026 (includes amendments up to Act No. 66, 2026), register id
-- C2026C00366, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/C2013A00020.txt. The deposit's caveat: a version in force from
-- 19 September 2026 had no registered compilation when it was retrieved, so later amendments may be missing.
-- The National Disability Insurance Scheme (Becoming a Participant) Rules 2016 are NOT deposited. What they prescribe for
-- ss 24 and 25 (s 27: "methods or criteria to be applied", circumstances in which a matter "is taken to exist or to not exist")
-- and for s 9B (functional capacity) is an INPUT: each s 24 and s 25 element is asked as the person's fact, as the rules would
-- assess it; the s 25(2) prescribed impairments and any s 20(2)(b) lesser number of days are inputs.
--
-- NOT ENCODED. Plans, supports, funding and plan management (Chapter 3, Parts 2 and 3); nominees and child representatives
-- (Chapter 4, Part 1 -- Ruby's role as attorney or guardian is a matter of the WA Guardianship and Administration Act 1990);
-- s 30A (the rules-prescribed reassessment); what is an NDIS support (s 10, asked as part of the s 24(1)(e) and s 25(1)(d)
-- facts); "Australian citizen", "permanent visa" and "special category visa" (Australian Citizenship Act and Migration Act
-- meanings, asked); "ongoing funded aged care service" and "specialist aged care program" (Aged Care Act 2024 meanings,
-- asked); further review under s 103; information, compensation, debts, providers, the Commission and penalties (Chapters 4,
-- 4A, 5). Machinery (the Agency, the Board, the rule-making power, commencement) is out.
--
-- Dates are written YYYYMMDD as numbers. Adding 650000 gives the 65th birthday (a 29 February birthday is not modelled).
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill, from the seat of the
-- individual to whom the law is applied, with the design defaults ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `National Disability Insurance Scheme Act 2013`

-- The 65th birthday of a person born on `born`, as YYYYMMDD.
GIVEN `born` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the 65th birthday of a person born on` MEANS
    `born` PLUS 650000

§§ `s 22 -- age requirements`

-- s 22: "A person meets the age requirements if the person was aged under 65 when the access request in relation to the
-- person was made." Gloss: the age is fixed on the day the request is made, not the day the CEO considers it (contrast
-- s 21(1)(b), (c): "at the time of considering the request"). Nothing in s 22 sets a lower age.
@export Do I meet the NDIS age requirements (s 22)?
GIVEN `my date of birth` IS A NUMBER @desc Your date of birth, as YYYYMMDD
      `the day I made the access request` IS A NUMBER @desc The day your access request was made, as YYYYMMDD
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I meet the age requirements` IF
    `the day I made the access request` LESS THAN `the 65th birthday of a person born on` `my date of birth`

§§ `s 23; s 9 -- residence requirements`

-- s 23(1): "A person meets the residence requirements if the person: (a) resides in Australia; and (b) is one of the
-- following: (i) an Australian citizen; (ii) the holder of a permanent visa; (iii) a special category visa holder who is a
-- protected SCV holder." Gloss: "permanent visa" and "special category visa" have the Migration Act 1958 meanings (s 9),
-- asked as facts. A special category visa is the visa a New Zealand citizen holds on arrival.
DECLARE `My status in Australia` IS ONE OF
    `an Australian citizen`
    `the holder of a permanent visa`
    `a special category visa holder`
    `none of these`

-- s 9: "a person is a protected SCV holder if: (a) the person was in Australia on 26 February 2001, and was a special
-- category visa holder on that day; or (b) the person had been in Australia for a period of, or for periods totalling, 12
-- months during the 2 years immediately before 26 February 2001, and returned to Australia after that day."
DECLARE `My residence` HAS
    `the CEO is satisfied I reside in Australia`                            IS A BOOLEAN
    `my status`                                                             IS A `My status in Australia`
    `I was in Australia on 26 February 2001`                                IS A BOOLEAN
    `I held a special category visa on 26 February 2001`                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `months I was in Australia in the 2 years before 26 February 2001`      IS A NUMBER
    `I returned to Australia after 26 February 2001`                        IS A BOOLEAN

@export Am I a protected SCV holder (s 9)?
GIVEN `r` IS A `My residence` @desc Where you were around 26 February 2001 and the visa you held then
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I a protected SCV holder` IF
        (`r`'s `I was in Australia on 26 February 2001` AND `r`'s `I held a special category visa on 26 February 2001`)
    OR  (`r`'s `months I was in Australia in the 2 years before 26 February 2001` AT LEAST 12
         AND `r`'s `I returned to Australia after 26 February 2001`)

-- s 23(2): "In deciding whether or not a person resides in Australia, regard must be had to: (a) the nature of the
-- accommodation ...; (b) ... family relationships ...; (c) ... employment, business or financial ties ...; (d) ... assets ...;
-- (e) the frequency and duration of the person's travel outside Australia; and (f) any other matter relevant to determining
-- whether the person intends to remain permanently in Australia." Those are the CEO's matters: residing is asked as the
-- CEO's satisfaction (s 21(1)(b)), "at the time of considering the request".
@export Do I meet the NDIS residence requirements (s 23)?
GIVEN `r` IS A `My residence` @desc Whether the CEO is satisfied you reside in Australia, and your citizenship or visa
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I meet the residence requirements` IF
    `r`'s `the CEO is satisfied I reside in Australia`
    AND (CONSIDER `r`'s `my status`
         WHEN `an Australian citizen` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `the holder of a permanent visa` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `a special category visa holder` THEN `Am I a protected SCV holder` `r`
         WHEN `none of these` THEN FALSE)

§§ `s 24 -- disability requirements`

-- s 24(1): "(a) the person has a disability that is attributable to one or more intellectual, cognitive, neurological,
-- sensory or physical impairments or the person has one or more impairments to which a psychosocial disability is
-- attributable; and (b) the impairment or impairments are, or are likely to be, permanent; and (c) the impairment or
-- impairments result in substantially reduced functional capacity in relation to one or more of the following activities
-- (considering each activity as a whole): (i) communication; (ii) social interaction; (iii) learning; (iv) mobility; (v)
-- self-care; (vi) self-management; and (d) the impairment or impairments affect the person's capacity for social or economic
-- participation; and (e) the person is likely to require NDIS supports under the National Disability Insurance Scheme for
-- the person's lifetime."
-- Gloss: "functional capacity" (s 9B) is the ability to do the activity without help, or only with commonly used assistive
-- technology, "in a context that excludes, as far as possible, the impact of the person's environmental and personal
-- circumstances". The Becoming a Participant Rules set the methods (s 27); not deposited, so each element is the person's
-- fact as those rules would assess it.
DECLARE `My disability` HAS
    `I have an intellectual, cognitive, neurological, sensory or physical impairment`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `I have an impairment to which a psychosocial disability is attributable`          IS A BOOLEAN
    `my impairments are, or are likely to be, permanent`                               IS A BOOLEAN
    `my impairments are episodic or fluctuating`                                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `the CEO takes my episodic or fluctuating impairments to be permanent`             IS A BOOLEAN
    `my capacity for communication is substantially reduced`                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `my capacity for social interaction is substantially reduced`                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `my capacity for learning is substantially reduced`                                IS A BOOLEAN
    `my capacity for mobility is substantially reduced`                                IS A BOOLEAN
    `my capacity for self-care is substantially reduced`                               IS A BOOLEAN
    `my capacity for self-management is substantially reduced`                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `my impairments affect my capacity for social or economic participation`           IS A BOOLEAN
    `I am likely to require NDIS supports for my lifetime`                             IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `d` IS A `My disability`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `I have an impairment of a kind the Act names` IF
        `d`'s `I have an intellectual, cognitive, neurological, sensory or physical impairment`
    OR  `d`'s `I have an impairment to which a psychosocial disability is attributable`

-- s 24(2): impairments "that vary in intensity may be permanent ... despite the variation" -- no deeming; answered by the
-- permanence fact. s 24(3): impairments "that are episodic or fluctuating may be taken to be permanent" -- "may": the CEO's
-- judgment, asked. s 25(1A) says the same for early intervention.
@export Are my impairments permanent, or taken to be (s 24(1)(b), (2), (3); s 25(1A))?
GIVEN `d` IS A `My disability` @desc Whether your impairments are permanent, or episodic and taken by the CEO to be permanent
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are my impairments permanent` IF
        `d`'s `my impairments are, or are likely to be, permanent`
    OR  (`d`'s `my impairments are episodic or fluctuating`
         AND `d`'s `the CEO takes my episodic or fluctuating impairments to be permanent`)

-- s 24(1)(c): "one or more" of the six activities.
GIVEN `d` IS A `My disability`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `my functional capacity is substantially reduced in at least one activity` IF
        `d`'s `my capacity for communication is substantially reduced`
    OR  `d`'s `my capacity for social interaction is substantially reduced`
    OR  `d`'s `my capacity for learning is substantially reduced`
    OR  `d`'s `my capacity for mobility is substantially reduced`
    OR  `d`'s `my capacity for self-care is substantially reduced`
    OR  `d`'s `my capacity for self-management is substantially reduced`

@export Do I meet the NDIS disability requirements (s 24)?
GIVEN `d` IS A `My disability` @desc Your impairments, their permanence and their effect on your functional capacity
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I meet the disability requirements` IF
        `I have an impairment of a kind the Act names` `d`
    AND `Are my impairments permanent` `d`
    AND `my functional capacity is substantially reduced in at least one activity` `d`
    AND `d`'s `my impairments affect my capacity for social or economic participation`
    AND `d`'s `I am likely to require NDIS supports for my lifetime`

§§ `s 25; s 9 -- early intervention requirements`

-- s 9: "child means a person who is under 18 years of age." "developmental delay means a delay in the development of a child
-- under 6 years of age that: (a) is attributable to a mental or physical impairment or a combination of mental and physical
-- impairments; and (b) results in substantial reduction in functional capacity in relation to one or more of the following
-- areas of major life activity: (i) self-care; (ii) receptive and expressive language; (iii) cognitive development; (iv)
-- motor development; and (c) results in the need for a combination and sequence of special interdisciplinary or generic
-- care, treatment or other services that are of extended duration and are individually planned and coordinated."
DECLARE `My development` HAS
    `my age in years`                                                                  IS A NUMBER
    `I have a delay in my development attributable to a mental or physical impairment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the delay substantially reduces my capacity in self-care, language, cognitive or motor development` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the delay needs individually planned and coordinated interdisciplinary services of extended duration` IS A BOOLEAN

@export Do I have developmental delay (s 9)?
GIVEN `v` IS A `My development` @desc Your age and the delay in your development
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I have developmental delay` IF
        `v`'s `my age in years` LESS THAN 6
    AND `v`'s `I have a delay in my development attributable to a mental or physical impairment`
    AND `v`'s `the delay substantially reduces my capacity in self-care, language, cognitive or motor development`
    AND `v`'s `the delay needs individually planned and coordinated interdisciplinary services of extended duration`

-- s 25(1)(b)-(d): "the CEO is satisfied that provision of early intervention supports for the person is likely to benefit the
-- person by reducing the person's future needs for supports in relation to disability"; "... by: (i) mitigating or
-- alleviating the impact of the person's impairment or impairments upon the person's functional capacity ...; or (ii)
-- preventing the deterioration of such functional capacity; or (iii) improving such functional capacity; or (iv)
-- strengthening the sustainability of informal supports available to the person, including through building the capacity
-- of the person's carer"; and "any early intervention supports that would be likely to benefit the person ... would be NDIS
-- supports for the person". All three are the CEO's satisfaction: inputs.
-- s 25(2): "The CEO is taken to be satisfied as mentioned in paragraphs (1)(b) and (c) if one or more of the person's
-- impairments are prescribed by the National Disability Insurance Scheme rules for the purposes of this subsection."
DECLARE `What the CEO is satisfied of about early intervention` HAS
    `early intervention would likely reduce my future needs for supports`             IS A BOOLEAN
    `early intervention would likely mitigate, prevent deterioration of, improve my functional capacity or sustain my informal supports` IS A BOOLEAN
    `those early intervention supports would be NDIS supports for me`                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `one of my impairments is prescribed by the NDIS rules for s 25(2)`               IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 25(1)(a): "(i) has one or more identified intellectual, cognitive, neurological, sensory or physical impairments that are,
-- or are likely to be, permanent; or (ii) has one or more identified impairments to which a psychosocial disability is
-- attributable and that are, or are likely to be, permanent; or (iii) is a child who has developmental delay". Note 1: a
-- person "with a degenerative condition could meet the early intervention requirements". Unlike s 24, no reduced functional
-- capacity, no lifetime need and no age limit apply to limbs (i) and (ii).
@export Do I meet the NDIS early intervention requirements (s 25)?
GIVEN `d` IS A `My disability` @desc Your impairments and whether they are permanent
      `v` IS A `My development` @desc Your age and any developmental delay
      `c` IS A `What the CEO is satisfied of about early intervention` @desc What the CEO is satisfied early intervention would do for you
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I meet the early intervention requirements` IF
        ((`I have an impairment of a kind the Act names` `d` AND `Are my impairments permanent` `d`)
         OR `Do I have developmental delay` `v`)
    AND (`c`'s `one of my impairments is prescribed by the NDIS rules for s 25(2)`
         OR (`c`'s `early intervention would likely reduce my future needs for supports`
             AND `c`'s `early intervention would likely mitigate, prevent deterioration of, improve my functional capacity or sustain my informal supports`))
    AND `c`'s `those early intervention supports would be NDIS supports for me`

§§ `ss 18, 21, 28 -- the access criteria, and the day I become a participant`

-- s 18: "A person may make a request (an access request) to the Agency to become a participant".
-- s 21(1): "A person meets the access criteria if: (a) the CEO is satisfied that the person meets the age requirements ...;
-- and (b) ... at the time of considering the request, the person meets the residence requirements ...; and (c) ... at the
-- time of considering the request: (i) the person meets the disability requirements ...; or (ii) the person meets the early
-- intervention requirements". (2): "the CEO must separately consider and decide" both.
DECLARE `My access request` HAS
    `my date of birth`                      IS A NUMBER
    `the day I made the request`            IS A NUMBER
    `my residence`                          IS A `My residence`
    `my disability`                         IS A `My disability`
    `my development`                        IS A `My development`
    `the CEO's view of early intervention`  IS A `What the CEO is satisfied of about early intervention`

@export Do I meet the access criteria to become an NDIS participant (s 21)?
GIVEN `a` IS A `My access request` @desc Your age, residence, disability and what the CEO is satisfied of
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I meet the access criteria` IF
        `Do I meet the age requirements` (`a`'s `my date of birth`) (`a`'s `the day I made the request`)
    AND `Do I meet the residence requirements` (`a`'s `my residence`)
    AND (    `Do I meet the disability requirements` (`a`'s `my disability`)
         OR  `Do I meet the early intervention requirements` (`a`'s `my disability`) (`a`'s `my development`) (`a`'s `the CEO's view of early intervention`))

-- s 28(2): the notice must state "(a) the date on which the person became a participant; and (b) whichever of the following
-- applies: (i) that the CEO is satisfied the participant meets the early intervention requirements; (ii) ... the disability
-- requirements; (iii) ... both".
DECLARE `What my notice says I meet` IS ONE OF
    `the early intervention requirements`
    `the disability requirements`
    `both the early intervention and the disability requirements`
    `I do not meet the access criteria`

@export Which requirements will my participant notice say I meet (ss 21(2), 28(2)(b))?
GIVEN `a` IS A `My access request` @desc Your age, residence, disability and what the CEO is satisfied of
GIVETH A `What my notice says I meet`
DECIDE `Which requirements will my notice say I meet` IS
    IF (NOT (`Do I meet the access criteria` `a`))
    THEN `I do not meet the access criteria`
    ELSE IF     `Do I meet the disability requirements` (`a`'s `my disability`)
            AND `Do I meet the early intervention requirements` (`a`'s `my disability`) (`a`'s `my development`) (`a`'s `the CEO's view of early intervention`)
         THEN `both the early intervention and the disability requirements`
         ELSE IF `Do I meet the disability requirements` (`a`'s `my disability`)
              THEN `the disability requirements`
              ELSE `the early intervention requirements`

-- s 28(1): "A person becomes a participant ... on the day the CEO decides that the person meets the access criteria."
-- Gloss: not the day of the request. A person who does not meet the criteria does not become one: 0 says so.
@export On what day do I become an NDIS participant (s 28(1))? 0 means not at all.
GIVEN `a` IS A `My access request` @desc Your age, residence, disability and what the CEO is satisfied of
      `the day the CEO decides` IS A NUMBER @desc The day the CEO decides your access request, as YYYYMMDD
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `On what day do I become a participant` IS
    IF `Do I meet the access criteria` `a` THEN `the day the CEO decides` ELSE 0

§§ `ss 20, 21(3), 26 -- how long the CEO has, and what silence means`

-- s 20(1): the CEO must "(a) decide whether or not the prospective participant meets the access criteria; or (b) make one or
-- more requests under subsection 26(1)". (2): within "(a) 90 days, unless paragraph (b) applies; (b) if the National Disability
-- Insurance Scheme rules prescribe a lesser number of days ... that lesser number of days". The rules' number is an input
-- (0 for none).
@export How many days does the CEO have to decide my access request or ask me for more (s 20(2))?
GIVEN `days prescribed by the NDIS rules` IS A NUMBER @desc A lesser number of days prescribed by the NDIS rules for s 20(2)(b), or 0 if none
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many days does the CEO have to act on my request` IS
    IF `days prescribed by the NDIS rules` GREATER THAN 0 AND `days prescribed by the NDIS rules` LESS THAN 90
    THEN `days prescribed by the NDIS rules`
    ELSE 90

-- s 26(2): if the information and reports asked for are received "within 90 days, or such longer period as is specified in
-- the request", the CEO must "within 14 days after the last information or report is received: (c) decide ...; or (d) make a
-- further request". (3): if not received in that period, "the prospective participant is taken to have withdrawn the access
-- request, unless the CEO is satisfied that it was reasonable ... not to have complied". s 21(3): the CEO "is taken to have
-- decided that the prospective participant does not meet the access criteria if: (a) the CEO does not do a thing referred to
-- in paragraph 20(1)(a) or (b) within the period applicable under section 20; or (b) if subsection 26(2) applies -- the CEO
-- does not do one of the things referred to in that subsection within the 14-day period".
DECLARE `Where my access request stands` HAS
    `days since the Agency received my request`                       IS A NUMBER
    `days prescribed by the NDIS rules`                               IS A NUMBER
    `the CEO decided or asked me for more within that time`           IS A BOOLEAN
    `the CEO asked me for information or reports`                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `days since the CEO asked`                                        IS A NUMBER
    `longer period the CEO's request allowed, in days`                IS A NUMBER
    `everything asked for has been received`                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `days it took for everything to be received`                      IS A NUMBER
    `days since the last of it was received`                          IS A NUMBER
    `the CEO decided or asked again within 14 days of receiving it`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the CEO is satisfied my not complying in time was reasonable`    IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `What has happened to my access request` IS ONE OF
    `it is still within time`
    `I am taken to be refused, and it will be reviewed automatically`
    `I am taken to have withdrawn it`
    `the CEO acted in time`

GIVEN `s` IS A `Where my access request stands`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the period for the information` MEANS
    IF `s`'s `longer period the CEO's request allowed, in days` GREATER THAN 90
    THEN `s`'s `longer period the CEO's request allowed, in days`
    ELSE 90

@export What has happened to my access request if the CEO has not decided it (ss 20, 21(3), 26(2), (3), 100(5))?
GIVEN `s` IS A `Where my access request stands` @desc How long it has been and what the CEO has asked for and received
GIVETH A `What has happened to my access request`
DECIDE `What has happened to my access request` IS
    IF (NOT (`s`'s `the CEO decided or asked me for more within that time`))
    THEN IF `s`'s `days since the Agency received my request` GREATER THAN `How many days does the CEO have to act on my request` (`s`'s `days prescribed by the NDIS rules`)
         THEN `I am taken to be refused, and it will be reviewed automatically`
         ELSE `it is still within time`
    ELSE IF (NOT (`s`'s `the CEO asked me for information or reports`))
         THEN `the CEO acted in time`
         ELSE IF `s`'s `everything asked for has been received` AND `s`'s `days it took for everything to be received` AT MOST `the period for the information` `s`
              THEN IF `s`'s `the CEO decided or asked again within 14 days of receiving it`
                   THEN `the CEO acted in time`
                   ELSE IF `s`'s `days since the last of it was received` GREATER THAN 14
                        THEN `I am taken to be refused, and it will be reviewed automatically`
                        ELSE `it is still within time`
              ELSE IF `s`'s `days since the CEO asked` AT MOST `the period for the information` `s`
                   THEN `it is still within time`
                   ELSE IF `s`'s `the CEO is satisfied my not complying in time was reasonable`
                        THEN `it is still within time`
                        ELSE `I am taken to have withdrawn it`

§§ `ss 100(2), 19(2) -- review, and asking again`

-- s 100(2): a person directly affected "may request the decision-maker to review the reviewable decision. If the person is
-- given a notice under subsection (1) the person must make the request within 3 months after receiving the notice."
-- INFERENCE: the 3 months end on the corresponding day of the third month after receipt; a day that does not exist in that
-- month (30 February) sorts after the last real day, so the month's end is in time and the next month is not.
GIVEN `d` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`three months after` MEANS
    IF `month` PLUS 3 GREATER THAN 12
    THEN (`year` PLUS 1) TIMES 10000 PLUS (`month` PLUS 3 MINUS 12) TIMES 100 PLUS `day`
    ELSE `year` TIMES 10000 PLUS (`month` PLUS 3) TIMES 100 PLUS `day`
    WHERE
        `year`  MEANS TRUNC (`d` DIVIDED BY 10000) 0
        `month` MEANS TRUNC ((`d` MINUS `year` TIMES 10000) DIVIDED BY 100) 0
        `day`   MEANS `d` MINUS `year` TIMES 10000 MINUS `month` TIMES 100

@export Am I in time to ask for a review of the access decision (s 100(2))?
GIVEN `the day I received the notice` IS A NUMBER @desc The day you received the notice of the decision, as YYYYMMDD
      `the day I ask for review` IS A NUMBER @desc The day you ask for the review, as YYYYMMDD
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I in time to ask for a review` IF
    `the day I ask for review` AT MOST `three months after` `the day I received the notice`

-- s 19(2): after a refusal (actual or deemed under s 21(3)) or a revocation, "the person may make another access request at
-- any time, unless at that time either of the following has been commenced, but not finally determined: (c) a review ...
-- under subsection 100(5) of the CEO's decision; (d) a review under section 103 of a decision on the initial review."
@export May I make another access request (s 19(2))?
GIVEN `I was refused or my participation was revoked` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the CEO refused (or is taken to have refused) your request, or revoked your participation
      `a review of that decision is under way` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a review under s 100(5) or s 103 has begun and is not finally decided
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I make another access request` IF
    `I was refused or my participation was revoked` AND (NOT `a review of that decision is under way`)

§§ `ss 29, 29A, 30 -- when I stop being a participant`

-- s 29(1): "A person ceases to be a participant ... when: (a) the person dies; or (b) the person commences accessing ongoing
-- funded aged care services on a permanent basis, other than under a specialist aged care program, and this first occurs
-- only after the person turns 65 years of age; or (c) the person's status as a participant is revoked under subsection 30(1)
-- or (5), paragraph 30A(1)(c) or subsection 30A(7); or (d) the person is taken to withdraw as a participant under subsection
-- 29A(5)."
-- Gloss: turning 65 is not on the list. Paragraph (b) needs permanent aged care that FIRST begins on or after the 65th
-- birthday (INFERENCE: "after the person turns 65" read as from the day of turning 65); permanent aged care begun before 65
-- does not end participation later. "Ongoing funded aged care service" and "specialist aged care program" have the Aged Care
-- Act 2024 meanings (s 9), asked.
DECLARE `My life as a participant` HAS
    `my date of birth`                                                         IS A NUMBER
    `I have died`                                                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `I access ongoing funded aged care services on a permanent basis`          IS A BOOLEAN
    `the day I first began accessing them on a permanent basis`                IS A NUMBER
    `I access them under a specialist aged care program`                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `my participant status has been revoked`                                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `I am taken to have withdrawn`                                             IS A BOOLEAN

@export Does going into aged care end my participation (s 29(1)(b))?
GIVEN `p` IS A `My life as a participant` @desc Your date of birth and any permanent aged care you receive
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does aged care end my participation` IF
        `p`'s `I access ongoing funded aged care services on a permanent basis`
    AND (NOT `p`'s `I access them under a specialist aged care program`)
    AND `p`'s `the day I first began accessing them on a permanent basis` AT LEAST `the 65th birthday of a person born on` (`p`'s `my date of birth`)

@export Have I ceased to be an NDIS participant (s 29(1))?
GIVEN `p` IS A `My life as a participant` @desc Your date of birth, aged care, and any revocation or withdrawal
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I ceased to be a participant` IF
        `p`'s `I have died`
    OR  `Does aged care end my participation` `p`
    OR  `p`'s `my participant status has been revoked`
    OR  `p`'s `I am taken to have withdrawn`

-- s 29(2): "A person is not entitled to be paid NDIS amounts so far as the amounts relate to supports that are acquired or
-- provided after the person ceases to be a participant." (3): the rules may say when supports are taken to be acquired or
-- provided before or after -- an input.
@export Can I be paid NDIS amounts for a support (s 29(2), (3))?
GIVEN `the day the support was acquired or provided` IS A NUMBER @desc The day of the support, as YYYYMMDD (as the NDIS rules under s 29(3) would date it)
      `the day I ceased to be a participant` IS A NUMBER @desc The day you ceased to be a participant, as YYYYMMDD, or 0 if you have not
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I be paid for the support` IF
        `the day I ceased to be a participant` EQUALS 0
    OR  `the day the support was acquired or provided` AT MOST `the day I ceased to be a participant`

-- s 29A(3): the cooling-off period "must not be less than 90 days beginning on the day the notice is given". (5): "If a
-- person does not cancel a request before the end of the cooling-off period, the person is taken to withdraw as a
-- participant at the end of that period." (4): the CEO may extend it.
@export What is the shortest cooling-off period I must be given if I ask to leave the NDIS, in days (s 29A(3))?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the shortest cooling-off period` IS 90

@export Am I taken to have withdrawn from the NDIS (s 29A(5))?
GIVEN `days since the CEO's notice was given` IS A NUMBER @desc Days since the CEO gave you the s 29A(2) notice, counting the day it was given as day 1
      `the cooling-off period in the notice, as extended, in days` IS A NUMBER @desc The cooling-off period stated in the notice, with any extension
      `I cancelled my request in time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you cancelled your request before the end of the cooling-off period
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I taken to have withdrawn` IF
        (NOT `I cancelled my request in time`)
    AND `days since the CEO's notice was given` GREATER THAN
            (IF `the cooling-off period in the notice, as extended, in days` LESS THAN 90
             THEN 90
             ELSE `the cooling-off period in the notice, as extended, in days`)

-- s 30(1): "The CEO may revoke a person's status as a participant ... if: (a) the CEO is satisfied that the person does not
-- meet the residence requirements ...; or (b) the CEO is satisfied that the person does not meet at least one of the
-- following: (i) the disability requirements ...; (ii) the early intervention requirements". Gloss: the age requirement is
-- not a ground -- it is fixed at the request (s 22), so ageing past 65 cannot be used to revoke.
-- (5), (6): if information or reports asked for under (3) are not received "within 90 days, or such longer period as is
-- specified in the request", the CEO "may revoke", but "must not ... if the CEO is satisfied that it was reasonable" not to
-- have complied.
DECLARE `My participation under review` HAS
    `the CEO is satisfied I no longer meet the residence requirements`               IS A BOOLEAN
    `the CEO is satisfied I meet neither the disability nor the early intervention requirements` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the CEO asked me for information or reports under s 30(3)`                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `I gave it all within 90 days or the longer period allowed`                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `the CEO is satisfied my not complying in time was reasonable`                   IS A BOOLEAN

@export May my NDIS participant status be revoked (s 30(1), (5), (6))?
GIVEN `r` IS A `My participation under review` @desc What the CEO is satisfied of and whether you answered a s 30(3) request in time
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my participant status be revoked` IF
        `r`'s `the CEO is satisfied I no longer meet the residence requirements`
    OR  `r`'s `the CEO is satisfied I meet neither the disability nor the early intervention requirements`
    OR  (    `r`'s `the CEO asked me for information or reports under s 30(3)`
         AND (NOT `r`'s `I gave it all within 90 days or the longer period allowed`)
         AND (NOT `r`'s `the CEO is satisfied my not complying in time was reasonable`))
